LineComment   "// Bounded projection: `T.X` where T is a generic parameter whose bound is an"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// interface that requires a readable member X. The projection resolves to X's"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// required read type — the bound version of read/projection symmetry. A"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// requirement typed `self` resolves to the parameter itself, and the value read"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// `v.X` on a value of type T resolves through the same bound, so the type-position"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// projection and the value read agree. A type parameter is a compile-time type,"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// not a value: it projects in type position (T.X) and reads off a value (v.X), but"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// is never consumed as a value itself."
Newline       "\n"
Newline       "\n"
